# ==================== CAR KEY PRESETS ====================
# Name = make + modulation + APPROX model-year era it covers. Modulation (OOK/FSK)
# comes from each decoder's own AM/FM flag, so the preset matches how that car reads.
# ** The year ranges are ROUGH GUIDES only ** — the OOK->FSK cutover varies by MODEL,
# TRIM and MARKET (US vs EU), not cleanly by make-year, so if the labeled era doesn't
# capture, try the make's other entry (the OOK<->FSK pair).
# Frequency is chosen SEPARATELY from the modulation: most = 433.92 MHz; N.America/
# Japan often 315 MHz; a few EU = 434.42 / 868.35 MHz (BMW/Mini EU FSK often 868.35).
# Notable quirks from research: Chrysler/Jeep/Dodge use 433.92 even in N.America
# post-'13; Honda older NA OOK is the oddball 313.85 MHz; VW/Audi/Porsche/Mercedes
# are ASK/OOK across eras (their FSK entries are rare fallbacks); Toyota/Lexus modern
# FSK often reads as OOK garbage on an ASK receiver (use the FSK preset).

